                <pb facs="0480" n="410" xml:id="pg410"/>

                <head>Mr. Plumb to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Orleans,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 27, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At 9 o’clock last evening, I received the
                    following telegraphic despatch from Mr. Marshall, the consul at Matamoros:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">[Via Galveston, May 26. Dated Matamoros, May 21, 1867.]</p>
                <p>To <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. L. Plumb,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">St. Charles Hotel, New Orleans:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to you the
                    following official letter:</p>
                <p rendition="#right">“<hi rendition="#small-caps">San Louis Potosi,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 15.</p>
                <p>“General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berriozabal</hi>:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">“My Esteemed Friend</hi>: Viva la patria!! Queretaro
                    has fallen by force of arms this a. m. at 8 o’clock. Maximilian, Mejia,
                    Castillo, and Miramon are prisoners.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">“BENITO JUAREZ.”</p>
                <p>Yours, truly,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">M.B. MARSHALL.</p>
                <p>The importance of the news it contained led me to transmit the despatch to you at
                    once by telegraph, as received.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, with the highest respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. L. PLUMB.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
